**Calculation:**

It is given that theta is an acute angle, So by trigonometric ratios-

sintheta = {{Perpendicular} over Hypotenuse} 

Since, sintheta = {{12} over 13} then on comparison,

⇒ **Hypotenuse = 13 unit and Perpendicular = 12 unit**

Now, by the Pythagorean theorem, 

(Hypotenuse)² = (perpendicular)² + (base)²

⇒ 13² = 12² + (base)²

⇒ (base)2 = 25

⇒ **base = 5 unit**

⇒ costheta={baseover hypontenuse} = {5over13}

⇒tantheta = {perpendicularover base}= {12over 5}

Substituting the values of sintheta, costheta and tantheta into the expression, 

⇒{((12)/(13))²-((5)/(13))² over 2.(12)/(13).(5)/(13)}times {1over ((12)/(5))²}

⇒{(119)/(169)over (120)/(169)}times {25over144}

⇒(119×25)/(120×144)= (119times 5)/(24times 144)

⇒{{595} over 3456} 

**The value of the expression is {{595} over 3456} **
